    "notice": "DEMONSTRATION GEOMETRY AND PARAMETERS. These polygons are coarse hand-drawn envelopes around real municipalities, not hydrological catchment boundaries or hazard maps. The parameters (ground level, drain invert, storage, pump capacity, barrier crest) are illustrative values chosen so the demonstration model behaves plausibly - they are NOT surveyed elevations or design capacities. Replace with DPWH/JICA catchment data and NAMRIA elevation before drawing any conclusion. For real hazard maps use the DOST Project NOAH / HazardHunterPH flood hazard layers. 'pondingConcentration' expresses that floodwater does not spread evenly: it collects in the low-lying fraction of each zone, so the depth people experience there is several times the mean water column. These multipliers are illustrative judgements, not measurements.",
